      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can identify some potentially trope-like characters in your list. Marcus feels like a classic \"tough guy with a heart of gold\" and Andre's \"restless hustler\" archetype leans heavily on the \"troubled young protagonist\" trope. \n\nMarcus and Andre might fit better in a gritty urban crime drama due to their rough-around-the-edges personas. In contrast, Julian and Elena seem like more fitting characters for a polished high-society drama, given their refined personas and association with wealth and elite social circles. Hiroshi, depending on how his character is developed, could work in either setting if his tech-savviness and discipline are presented as unique skills rather than relying on a familiar tech-wizard trope.",
